a Nelson, the state school official who won her primary, has raised a modest sum and has little cash remaining, though national Democrats have signaled late interest in investing here.\n\nNo public general-election polling exists, so the outlook rests on district fundamentals, money, and expert assessments, all of which favor the incumbent. An independent candidate on the ballot is unlikely to alter the outcome. The race is rated Likely Republican, with Nelson needing an unusual late shift to make it competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}]}